# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Ported from netlify.toml. Order matters: first match wins.

# Vanity short links for a resume or email signature.
/resume    /resume.pdf                        302
/linkedin  https://www.linkedin.com/in/mdonn  302

# The nav reads "Portfolio" / "About" / "Contact", but the tabs are hash-routed,
# so the real addresses carry a "#". Anyone typing the path directly — or any
# client that drops the fragment from a link — would otherwise hit a 404.
/about      /#about      302
/portfolio  /#portfolio  302
/contact    /#contact    302

# Anything else falls through to 404.html, which Cloudflare serves automatically.
#
# NOTE: no `/* /index.html 200` catch-all here.
# Netlify needs that line for SPA fallback. Cloudflare rejects it (error 100324,
# infinite loop) because Pages already strips `.html` and `/index` itself, so the
# rule re-triggers on its own output and fails the deploy.
